blocks.text:
Tel-haresha.The first of these variations only exists in the translation;
the original being uniformly
[Têl Charshâ ,] {Tel-harsha:}
the latter simply arises from the insertion of a [Vâv,] {wav;}
being written ['Addân ,] {Addan,} in
the parallel passage, and ['Addôwn ,]
{Addon,} here.

in their kingdom.Instead of {bemalkuthom,} "in their kingdom," {bemalkuthecha,}
"in thy kingdom," is the reading of two of Dr. Kennicott's
MSS., LXX., Syriac, and Arabic.

Sallu.The variation of [Callûw ,] Sallu,
and [Callay ,] Sallai, is simply
caused by the mutation of [Vâv,] {wav} and [Yôwd,] {yood.}
